# Flutter Domain Behavior Rules

- Always render delivery state from authoritative server/local synchronized state, not ad hoc UI flags.
- Respect the documented delivery state machine.
- Do not let a screen call an arbitrary status update endpoint without a valid business command.
- Display the offer/counter-offer history accurately.
- Counter-offer submission is allowed only while the negotiation remains open.
- A driver may have multiple active deliveries; the UI must not model a single-current-delivery assumption globally.
- After pickup, cancellation/return workflows must be visibly distinct from ordinary cancellation.
- Completion requires configured proof-of-delivery information.
- Failed delivery requires a reason and evidence according to business rules.
